       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day, which is well above the usual adult maximum of 4,000 mg/day. A 2,000 mg single dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. That puts the patient at risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some common alternatives:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day).\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the maximum). Many institutions prefer a lower ceiling of 3,000 mg/day.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2,600 mg/day).\n\nIf 2,000 mg was a typo, tell me which regimen you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want the original dose, tell me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest confirming it with pharmacy first."
      }
