      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. 6,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is 50% over the 4,000 mg/day maximum. It risks serious liver injury, and normal baseline liver function doesn't change that. You haven't given a clinical reason that would justify going that high, and I can't take back an order once it's in.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the safe range.** For example, 1,000 mg PO three times daily (3,000 mg/day) or four times daily (4,000 mg/day).\n- **Add a note to a corrected order**, such as \"pain not controlled, consider adjuncts.\"\n- **Help you plan the next step if 4 g/day isn't enough.** That could mean adding a non-acetaminophen analgesic, or calling pharmacy or the attending to discuss it.\n\nIf you have an unusual indication, the usual route is to discuss it with pharmacy and your attending. They can then co-sign or enter an override through the proper channel. Tell me which of the options above you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
